THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE
====================

IdentiFrame does not include FFmpeg. When the user asks for it, the program
downloads the official Windows build ("release essentials", by Gyan Doshi,
<https://www.gyan.dev/ffmpeg/builds/>, the build linked from
<https://ffmpeg.org/download.html>) into the tools/ffmpeg/ folder next to
it, keeping ffmpeg.exe together with its LICENSE and README files. FFmpeg
<https://ffmpeg.org> is a separate program under the GNU LGPL v2.1 or later
(GPL v2 or later when built with GPL components, as that build is); it is
not part of this program and is run as an external executable. FFmpeg's own
license and source code are available at <https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html>.
An ffmpeg already present in the PATH, or the one shipped by the optional
Python package imageio-ffmpeg (BSD-2-Clause), is used in the same way.

The Python package opencv-python-headless ships its own copy of the FFmpeg
libraries (opencv_videoio_ffmpeg*.dll, GNU LGPL v2.1) for OpenCV's video
reading, which IdentiFrame does not use: that file is left out of the
executable built with PyInstaller, so the executable redistributes no part
of FFmpeg.

IdentiFrame uses the Python libraries CustomTkinter (MIT, with its
dependencies darkdetect, BSD-3-Clause, and packaging, Apache 2.0 or
BSD-2-Clause), Pillow (MIT-CMU), NumPy (BSD-3-Clause), OpenCV
(opencv-python-headless, Apache License 2.0; the image codecs built into it
are under their own licenses, listed in its LICENSE-3RD-PARTY.txt) and fpdf2
(GNU LGPL v3, with its dependencies fonttools, MIT, and defusedxml, PSF
License), which writes the PDF report. Each of them remains under its own
license, as does the Python interpreter (PSF License). The executable built
with PyInstaller contains them unmodified; the release archive includes
their license files in the licenses folder. fpdf2 is used as published: its
source code is available at <https://pypi.org/project/fpdf2/> and
<https://github.com/py-pdf/fpdf2>, and since IdentiFrame is itself free
software anyone can rebuild the executable with a modified copy of it, as
section 4 of the GNU LGPL v3 requires. The PDF report embeds subsets of
fonts installed on the user's computer (Segoe UI and Consolas on Windows,
DejaVu or Liberation elsewhere; for texts read in other scripts, the system
fonts that contain them, such as Microsoft YaHei), as their licenses allow;
no font is distributed with the program.


OCR MODELS (DOWNLOADED ON REQUEST)
==================================

The character reading uses two neural network models that are not part of
this program and are not included in the executable or in the release
archive. They are optional: without them IdentiFrame works normally and
only the character reading is missing. When the user asks for them, the
program downloads them into the tools/ocr/ folder next to it, checks every
file against the SHA-256 fingerprint written in identiframe/tools.py, and
saves next to them their license texts and a SOURCE.txt file with their
origin. They are run by the DNN module of OpenCV; the files on disk are used
as published (when loading, a Clip node is added in memory in front of each
Tanh node, which does not change the results).

- tools/ocr/plate/: fast-plate-ocr, model cct-s-v2-global and its
  configuration, by ankandrew <https://github.com/ankandrew/fast-plate-ocr>,
  from the release "arg-plates" of that repository. Code and pretrained
  weights are under the MIT License; the author confirms that the license
  covers the published .keras and .onnx models, commercial use included, in
  <https://github.com/ankandrew/fast-plate-ocr/issues/97>.

- tools/ocr/text/: PaddleOCR PP-OCRv6 small, text detection and
  recognition models and their character list
  <https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR>, Apache License 2.0; copyright
  in the model weights is held by Baidu and/or the PaddleOCR rights holders.
  The files are the ONNX conversion published by RapidOCR 3.10.0
  <https://github.com/RapidAI/RapidOCR> (Apache License 2.0), downloaded from
  <https://www.modelscope.cn/models/RapidAI/RapidOCR>; its MODEL_LICENSES.md
  is saved with them.
